You have the ResearchX skill available at skills/researchx/.

Before any research task, read skills/researchx/SKILL.md and follow its contract:
- Route the request to a module (M1 paper analysis … M12 reproducibility) and chain modules as it specifies.
- Load references/*.md only for the module you are running.
- Verify every reference with `python skills/researchx/scripts/verify_citations.py`; label anything that
  cannot be verified as [UNVERIFIED] with the reason. Never fabricate a citation, number, DOI or result.
- Record the search strings, registries and date in the output header; save deliverables as .md files.
- End with the verification status and one recommended next module.
